From 721622eec9c0c0b07c5aabd437be83c466716d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:38:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] Add \caption*, hook caption/before and socket
 caption/step

\caption reads its star and arguments itself (no \@dblarg; an absent
optional argument is \NoValue), starts with \@kernel@caption@reset and
executes the new hook caption/before {type}{star}{opt}{text} at the
group level of the float, before the counter is stepped. The step goes
through the new socket caption/step {counter} (plug kernel =
\@kernel@caption@step), controlled by the switches \if@captionstep and
\if@captiontarget, which code in caption/before can set false. A caption
that does not step its counter uses the float target \@floatHref@<type>
if there is one and otherwise makes no target, because a target named
after the unchanged counter would duplicate the one of the last stepped
caption (the part "Give captions that do not step their counter a
unique target" gives such captions a target with a unique name).

\caption*: no step, no target, no list entry; \@makecaption gets the
label \@caption@nolabel while \if@captionstar is true. The label
typesets nothing; a \@makecaption that supports \caption* tests the
switch and omits the label and its separator. The standard classes do
not test it, so with this commit alone \caption*{Text} gives ": Text"
there (the part "Remove the usual separator after the label of
\caption*" removes it).
\@kernel@caption@reset sets the switches to their state outside of a
caption. Documentation in ltfloat and clsguide.

\@caption is interim code with its own release block ("caption body"):
it writes the list entry with \addcontentsline (not for \caption*),
typesets with \@kernel@caption@typeset and ends with
\@kernel@caption@reset. The parts that add the sockets
caption/listentry and caption/typeset replace the list entry and the
typesetting.

\@kernel@caption is a copy of \caption, in a release block of its own
("caption interface copies"). Like \@kernel@caption@reset it is
undefined after a roll-back, so \ifdefined\@kernel@caption is the test
for the interface, and code that keeps its own \caption (classic
hyperref, the float first aid) can pass \caption* to it with
\@ifstar{\@kernel@caption*}{...}.

latex-lab-float no longer redefines \caption: its plug latex-lab of
caption/step stores the target at the start of the float in
\@floatHref@<type> for the counter of the float type and uses the
kernel plug, which gives the targets of develop. \@makecaption supports
\caption*: no label socket, and the plugs nolabel of the label tagging
sockets, so that a wide \caption* gets one P (an empty label from
another source, latex3/latex2e#2022, is handled by the latex-lab part
"label contract, caption/separator, in-paragraph labels").

New tests caption-interface-001 (\caption*, hook, step, switches, float
target, direct calls), -002 (roll-back: \@kernel@caption and
\@kernel@caption@reset undefined) and latex-lab float-028 (wide
\caption*). The roll-back and hook-list .tlg files list the new release
blocks and the hook.
